+/* ---- the skinning programs ----
+ * Two vertex programs, after the Xbox prototype's (docs/xbox_proto/CHARACTERS.md): one blends two bones a vertex
+ * (48 instructions), one four (56). Both stay loaded in the program store (136 instructions) and a draw picks one
+ * by its start address. Source: platform/xbox/shaders/skin2.vp and skin4.vp in the application's tree, assembled
+ * with nxdk's tools/vp20compiler.
+ *
+ * Inputs: position, normal, colour, texture coordinates as for gliDirectDraw; attribute 10 (texture coordinates
+ * 1): four shorts, each a bone's constant offset (3 x its index in the palette of the draw); attribute 11: four
+ * float weights. Constants (c[0] is NV2A constant 96; the fixed-function state below it is untouched):
+ *   c[0..3]    model to screen (viewport x projection x modelview), its rows
+ *   c[4..6]    model to eye (the modelview's upper three rows): the normal, and the fog's eye depth
